# Plain Language

Use this style when writing docs, specs, READMEs, PR descriptions, issues, comments, and any other prose in this repo or on GitHub.

## Rules

- Use simple words. Pick the shortest word that still means the right thing.
- Be concise. Cut every word that does not add a fact.
- Stick to facts. State what is true. Skip opinion, hype, and hedging.
- No semicolons. Use a period or a new line instead.
- No filler words. Cut "just", "really", "basically", "in order to", "it is important to note".
- No em dashes. Use a period, comma, or parentheses instead.
- Sacrifice grammar for brevity. Fragments are fine. Drop articles when clear.
- Say only what is needed. Skip consequences, rationale, and context the reader already has.

## Examples

```markdown
# Bad
In order to get started, you'll need to install dependencies — this is really
important; without them, the server won't run.

# Good
Install dependencies first.
```

```markdown
# Bad
This PR basically refactors the session layer in order to improve maintainability.

# Good
Refactors the session layer.
```

```markdown
# Bad
The operator can register workspaces and delegate work to durable agent sessions — all through a local web console.

# Good
The operator registers workspaces. Work goes to durable agent sessions. The local web console controls both.
```
